WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.000
Some microbes that make methane look just like bacteria under a microscope.

2
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:15.560
In 1977, two scientists compared one molecule inside them.

3
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:21.240
They read the scores as evidence that these microbes form a separate line of

4
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:26.300
descent. How has DNA changed the way we classify life?

5
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.840
And why is it fine for science to change its mind?

6
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:36.313
Classification is the sorting of living things into groups, based on how they are

7
00:00:36.313 --> 00:00:41.213
related. The groups are nested, like folders inside folders.

8
00:00:42.053 --> 00:00:43.813
A kingdom is a large group.

9
00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:48.033
A domain is the largest group of all, above kingdom.

10
00:00:49.053 --> 00:00:54.753
A microscope shows shape and size, which is what people could see, but not ancestry.

11
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:59.433
Every cell builds proteins on ribosomes.

12
00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:04.353
Ribosomal RNA is the RNA that forms much of a ribosome.

13
00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:09.753
Because every cell has it, it can be compared across all cellular life.

14
00:01:10.693 --> 00:01:15.653
Its sequence changes slowly, so even distant groups still share enough of it to

15
00:01:15.653 --> 00:01:19.053
compare. Shared does not mean identical.

16
00:01:19.673 --> 00:01:21.593
The small differences are the evidence.

17
00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:29.517
Woese and Fox cut ribosomal RNA into short pieces and listed them for each organism.

18
00:01:30.097 --> 00:01:33.477
Then they scored how much two lists overlapped.

19
00:01:34.077 --> 00:01:38.597
The score runs from zero, no overlap, to one, the same.

20
00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:44.677
Methane-making microbes scored high with each other, and low with typical bacteria.

21
00:01:45.737 --> 00:01:50.217
In 1977, they read this as three major lines of descent.

22
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:56.010
In 1990, the rank of domain was proposed, above kingdom.

23
00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:00.910
The three domains are Bacteria, Archaea and Eukarya.

24
00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:07.030
Archaea are single-celled microbes that differ from bacteria in their RNA and

25
00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.330
membranes. Eukarya are organisms whose cells have a nucleus.

26
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:16.570
Fungi grow in place and have cell walls, so they look plant-like.

27
00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:25.410
But in 1993, a survey of 25 proteins strongly supported fungi being closer to animals than to plants.

28
00:02:26.283 --> 00:02:29.923
So why is it fine for science to change its mind?

29
00:02:30.703 --> 00:02:33.543
A classification is a claim about ancestry.

30
00:02:34.223 --> 00:02:38.743
A good claim can be tested, and some tests show it needs fixing.

31
00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:42.643
The older groups were reasonable for the evidence of their time.

32
00:02:43.323 --> 00:02:46.643
New DNA and RNA evidence changed the groups.

33
00:02:47.863 --> 00:02:50.163
Classification changes when the evidence changes.
